#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129004 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0118bf72-c730-59f1-b722-85ed779f96c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Speed of a Particle Given Its Velocity"}] :question/id #uuid "b776ff14-81d8-5e5d-8ea4-15969eb3904e" :question/math-academy-id "e-9816" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant velocity of $\\mathbf{u}=(5\\mathbf{i} +2\\mathbf{j}) \\,\\textrm{km/h}$. Find the speed of the particle." :question/worked-solution "The speed of a particle equals the magnitude of its velocity.\n\nTherefore, the speed of the particle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n\\begin{vmatrix}u & &= & 5i + 2j\\end{vmatrix} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{5^{2} + 2^{2}} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{25 + 4} \\\\\n&= \\sqrt{29}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nkilometers per hour."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129005 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5146ef7-bd48-5d0d-903d-882d739b92c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle"}] :question/id #uuid "33aad515-8d28-57f4-8d3e-448eb905324c" :question/math-academy-id "e-9817" :question/problem "A particle moves with constant acceleration. When $t=0 \\, \\textrm{h}$, the velocity of the particle is $4\\mathbf{i} \\, \\textrm{km/h}$, and when $t=3\\, \\textrm{h}$, the velocity of the particle is $(7\\mathbf{i}+15\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}$. Calculate the acceleration of the particle." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{u} = 4\\mathbf{i}, \\qquad \\mathbf{v} = 7\\mathbf{i}+15\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad t =3\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $\\mathbf{a}$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= u + at \\\\\n7i + 15j &= 4i + a(3) \\\\\n3i + 15j &= 3a \\\\\na &= \\frac{1}{3}(3i + 15j) \\\\\na &= (i + 5j)km/h^{2}\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129006 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/id #uuid "bf9ee32f-b32c-5acc-90f7-c2daf10b2497" :question/math-academy-id "e-9818" :question/problem "The velocity of a particle is $(\\mathbf{i} -4\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{m/s}$ when $t=0\\,\\textrm{s}$. If the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{m/s}^2$, find the velocity of the particle when $t=5 \\, \\textrm{s}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nHere, we have\n\n$$\n\\mathbf u = \\mathbf{i} -4\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf a = 2\\mathbf{i}+\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\nTherefore, after\n\n$$\nt = 5 \\, \\textrm{s}\n$$\n\nthe velocity of the particle will be\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= u + at \\\\\n&= (i - 4j) + (2i + j)(5) \\\\\n&= (i - 4j) + (10i + 5j) \\\\\n&= (11i + j)m/s\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129007 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "93d45138-b681-55c0-8910-1400bdf717c5" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Time when a Particle Reaches a Particular Velocity"}] :question/id #uuid "e2aff165-10d7-5d4d-9058-a15121222ebe" :question/math-academy-id "e-9819" :question/problem "A particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(\\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}^2$. The velocity of the particle is $(-\\mathbf{i} - \\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}$ when $t=0\\,\\textrm{h}$. Find the time when the velocity of the particle equals $(3\\mathbf{i}+7\\mathbf{j}) \\, \\textrm{km/h}$." :question/worked-solution "Recall that when a particle moves with constant acceleration, the velocity vector at time $t$ can be found using\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{v} = \\mathbf{u} + \\mathbf{a}t\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf{u}$ is the initial velocity, and $\\mathbf{a}$ is the acceleration of the particle.\n\nSubstituting\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{a} = \\mathbf{i} + 2\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf{u} = -\\mathbf{i} -\\mathbf{j}, \\qquad \\mathbf{v} = 3\\mathbf{i}+7\\mathbf{j}\n$$\n\ninto the equation above, we can solve for $t$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nv &= u + at \\\\\n3i + 7j &= (-i - j) + (i + 2j)t \\\\\n4i + 8j &= (i + 2j)t \\\\\n4i + 8j &= ti + 2tj\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the $\\mathbf i$ and $\\mathbf j$ components in the last equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n{4 = t; 8 = 2t\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129413 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7439a96f-07b1-5673-a103-af2c63c25d18" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Final Velocity of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a86be3a0-5f3d-5916-b018-57e814acb0fe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126285} {:answer/id #uuid "d8efeca6-1dc7-5d48-baa8-40e304d0174a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126286} {:answer/id #uuid "2acecd81-38ca-5857-9bb4-f1cdf2130911" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126287} {:answer/id #uuid "2ce0a77a-f796-56c7-9060-846bea0068d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{67}km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126288} {:answer/id #uuid "4fc50632-cc77-572f-a514-bfb2c8d1de03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{74}km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126289}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4fc50632-cc77-572f-a514-bfb2c8d1de03" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{74}km/h" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126289} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1e85e48-0b95-5207-8ad4-63989ca5b6f4" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126284}] :question/id #uuid "de06da58-c21f-5b57-9d0e-aa8b476e4cc8" :question/math-academy-id "q-136288" :question/problem "> A scientific calculator is required to answer this question.\n\nThe initial velocity of a particle is $(5i - j)km/h$. Find the speed of the particle after $2$ hours if the particle moves with a constant acceleration of $(i + 3j)km/h^{2}$." :question/requires-calculator true}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186129414 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "c5146ef7-bd48-5d0d-903d-882d739b92c7" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Acceleration of a Particle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d4672d49-ed68-5749-af07-6551eb7fbbe1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2i + 4j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126291} {:answer/id #uuid "246893e9-8f38-5719-90f9-e5359a2f8b2a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i - 2j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126292} {:answer/id #uuid "391f27a5-4c27-5b93-be93-463a8369ec52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i + 2j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126293} {:answer/id #uuid "5fea3226-571f-5dcb-86c8-5248838fabcf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126294} {:answer/id #uuid "7c97e288-29da-529f-b1fe-9e0ff3367ca0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4im/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126295}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "391f27a5-4c27-5b93-be93-463a8369ec52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(i + 2j)m/s^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126293} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccfed89d-b25d-5449-a46c-bd5f21d33670" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186126290}] :question/id #uuid "1d30498e-7